WEBVTT

00:01.517 --> 00:05.078
тЩк It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.111 --> 00:08.372
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.405 --> 00:11.966
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.999 --> 00:14.961
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.994 --> 00:18.454
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.486 --> 00:22.014
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:22.048 --> 00:23.611
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.645 --> 00:25.109
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:25.143 --> 00:30.533
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.293 --> 00:35.590
Previously on Family Guy...

00:35.623 --> 00:37.254
Certain of his own wit
and intellect,

00:37.287 --> 00:39.583
Brian opened up
a Twitter account.

00:39.617 --> 00:42.112
If you ask me, Twitter is
the perfect place for that guy,

00:42.145 --> 00:43.842
because he's a twit.

00:43.875 --> 00:46.637
But an off-color tweet
suddenly made Brian

00:46.670 --> 00:48.833
a pariah to all of Quahog,

00:48.866 --> 00:50.962
forcing the family
to make the difficult choice

00:50.996 --> 00:53.158
of sending him
to a crappy apartment

00:53.191 --> 00:54.690
on the other side of town.

00:56.186 --> 00:58.149
Brian, the family has spoken.

00:58.183 --> 01:00.146
You know,
you're the only man in America

01:00.180 --> 01:02.442
who looks good
in sandals and cargo shorts.

01:02.476 --> 01:04.772
Good luck, everyone.
I'll miss you.

01:04.805 --> 01:06.601
Uhp, something's comin'!

01:09.296 --> 01:11.593
Brian. Brian!

01:11.625 --> 01:14.055
I said you're a week late
on your rent.

01:14.088 --> 01:16.017
Well, I can get you the money.
Hang-hang on.

01:16.051 --> 01:18.081
Let me just make a call.

01:18.113 --> 01:19.911
Hello. You've reached...

01:19.945 --> 01:21.750
- The Griffins!
- Chris!

01:21.774 --> 01:23.746
See that? I told you
we should've rehearsed this.

01:23.770 --> 01:25.068
Lois, can we do it over?

01:25.101 --> 01:26.533
No, that's eight times.

01:26.566 --> 01:28.761
- Just leave a message.
- I'm sorry.

01:28.794 --> 01:30.226
Hey, guys.

01:30.259 --> 01:32.522
It's me again. Brian.

01:32.555 --> 01:34.684
We haven't talked
since I moved out,

01:34.718 --> 01:37.480
so I figured, you know, 10:00,

01:37.514 --> 01:40.674
you're probably on the couch
watching Pawn Stars.

01:40.707 --> 01:43.235
So, uh, pick up.

01:43.268 --> 01:45.997
Pick up?

01:46.030 --> 01:48.293
Uh, da, da, da, da, da, da.

01:48.326 --> 01:50.523
Maybe you went out.

01:50.556 --> 01:52.520
Da, da, da, da, da, da.

01:52.553 --> 01:54.815
Da, da, da...

01:54.848 --> 01:56.944
Ooh-wa, ooh...

01:56.978 --> 01:58.940
Okay. Well, again, it's Brian.

01:58.974 --> 02:01.170
Um, guys, really,
really, call me back.

02:01.203 --> 02:03.100
It's Brian. Bye.

02:03.133 --> 02:04.365
So, what do you think?

02:04.398 --> 02:06.059
Is your family gonna give you
money for the rent?

02:06.061 --> 02:07.126
Yeah, I'm thinking no.

02:07.160 --> 02:08.690
Well, you got to do something,
Brian.

02:08.723 --> 02:10.488
- You're a week behind.
- Okay, okay.

02:10.521 --> 02:11.984
Look, I'll get a job, okay?

02:12.017 --> 02:13.848
There's got to be something
I can do.

02:13.881 --> 02:15.645
It's not like I'm Ringo.

02:15.678 --> 02:17.907
Well, lads, what do you think
of the new album cover?

02:17.941 --> 02:21.435
Great, but it won't look good
when it's shrunk down for a CD.

02:21.468 --> 02:23.431
CD? What's a CD?

02:23.464 --> 02:25.892
A digital compact disc.

02:25.926 --> 02:27.889
Ringo, are you from the future?

02:27.923 --> 02:29.952
Yeah. And I outlive two of you.

02:29.985 --> 02:32.448
- Which two?
- Yeah, come on, Ringo. Tell us.

02:32.481 --> 02:36.940
Okay, but you all have to agree
to do my song about the octopus.

02:36.972 --> 02:38.271
Hey, before you tell us,

02:38.305 --> 02:40.134
I'm gonna go and smoke
a thousand cigarettes.

02:40.167 --> 02:42.097
And I'm gonna move
to New York City

02:42.130 --> 02:44.427
and walk in and out
of my building.

02:48.453 --> 02:51.846
Okay, everybody, time to go
to Grandma and Grandpa's house.

02:51.880 --> 02:53.942
- They're dead.
- Not your grandparents, Peter.

02:53.976 --> 02:55.407
I'm talking
about my parents.

02:55.440 --> 02:56.605
I hate going there.

02:56.637 --> 02:58.833
I'm not allowed to touch
anything in their house.

02:58.867 --> 03:01.263
And, besides, today's
Dolph Lundgren's birthday,

03:01.296 --> 03:03.026
and me and the guys
always celebrate it

03:03.060 --> 03:04.224
by watching Rocky IV.

03:04.258 --> 03:06.487
Fine, we're probably
better off without you.

03:06.520 --> 03:09.582
You always find a way
to embarrass us at my parents'.

03:11.611 --> 03:13.375
Please pass the All Fruit.

03:14.905 --> 03:16.901
Pass the Polaner All Fruit.

03:18.200 --> 03:19.476
Pass the Polaner All Fruit.

03:21.261 --> 03:23.358
Would you please pass the jelly?

03:30.544 --> 03:34.437
Hi. We're concerned that many
of you Family Guy fans under 40

03:34.470 --> 03:35.868
didn't get that reference,

03:35.902 --> 03:39.196
so I'm gonna take you
through the actual commercial.

03:39.229 --> 03:41.192
Okay, typical '80s
stuffy brunch.

03:41.225 --> 03:42.989
Please pass the All Fruit.

03:43.022 --> 03:45.118
Clearly the matriarch.
She's got the most pearls.

03:45.151 --> 03:46.316
Pass the Polaner All Fruit.

03:46.349 --> 03:48.146
Weird sexual tension there.

03:48.180 --> 03:50.176
Pass the Polaner All Fruit.

03:50.209 --> 03:52.204
Okay, okay, watch. Here's
where it all goes to hell.

03:52.206 --> 03:53.944
Would you please pass the jelly?

03:53.968 --> 03:55.808
See? He called it jelly.

03:55.832 --> 03:58.128
See... All right, now,
what I don't get is,

03:58.162 --> 03:59.658
if they know this guy,
why are they surprised

03:59.659 --> 04:01.653
by the way he talks? Right?

04:01.655 --> 04:04.450
And if they don't know him,
why is he at the table?

04:04.483 --> 04:06.114
Okay, now you have
the information

04:06.148 --> 04:09.308
that would've made that funny
had you had it going in.

04:13.335 --> 04:15.631
All right,
you ready to watch Rocky IV?

04:15.664 --> 04:18.758
- Let's do it!  -Yeah!
- Happy Dolph Lundgren Day!

04:20.787 --> 04:22.252
What the... what the hell?

04:22.285 --> 04:23.583
Try blowing on it.

04:28.142 --> 04:30.437
Crap! It
doesn't work!

04:30.470 --> 04:32.899
Well, we got to watch the movie.
It's our tradition.

04:32.932 --> 04:34.862
We could just stream it
on your Apple TV.

04:34.896 --> 04:37.358
Is that what that is?
I thought it was a coaster.

04:37.392 --> 04:39.853
I've been putting cold,
wet things on it for a month.

04:39.887 --> 04:43.082
Turn it on. I'm sure we
can find Rocky IV on there.

04:45.078 --> 04:47.474
I don't know how to turn it on.
It doesn't have any buttons.

04:47.506 --> 04:49.037
Well, maybe
it's voice-activated.

04:49.071 --> 04:52.564
Rocky IV! Rocky IV!

04:53.563 --> 04:55.160
Let's just go to
the damn store.

04:55.193 --> 04:58.720
Hold on, hold on, let me try
screaming at the PlayStation.

05:02.380 --> 05:04.276
Hey, you guys,
why the long faces?

05:04.309 --> 05:06.274
Eh, we were trying
to watch Rocky IV

05:06.307 --> 05:07.937
and our DVD didn't work.

05:07.970 --> 05:09.600
And that's just Scottie Pippen.

05:09.634 --> 05:11.032
When I was a baby,

05:11.065 --> 05:14.824
they pulled me out of my moms
real slow.

05:14.857 --> 05:16.323
We got a bin of old movies.

05:16.356 --> 05:18.185
Rocky IV might be in there.

05:19.217 --> 05:20.214
Let's see.

05:20.215 --> 05:22.078
Talladega Nights,
everywhere.

05:22.112 --> 05:24.174
Ladybugs, classic Rodney.

05:24.208 --> 05:27.169
A Million Ways to Die
in the West, no, thank you.

05:27.203 --> 05:29.498
Here it is! Rocky IV!

05:32.194 --> 05:35.155
Aw, nuts,
this one's written in terrorism.

05:35.189 --> 05:36.785
That's, uh, Cyrillic.

05:36.818 --> 05:38.383
It's a Russian bootleg.

05:38.416 --> 05:40.744
All right, we'll take it.
It's better than nothing.

05:40.778 --> 05:43.140
Hey!

05:47.999 --> 05:50.961
Welcome aboard, Brian.
This is your coworker, Martha.

05:55.618 --> 05:57.082
Pleased to meet
you, Brian.

05:57.115 --> 05:59.710
Pleasure's all mine.
So, any advice?

05:59.744 --> 06:02.273
Well, there's a script
you can go off of, if you want.

06:02.306 --> 06:04.901
Ah, script.
Now you're talking my language.

06:04.935 --> 06:06.399
Writer.

06:06.433 --> 06:09.228
So, watch out, or you might
end up in one of my scripts.

06:09.261 --> 06:11.058
"Martha, gorgeous, headstrong,

06:11.091 --> 06:13.685
legs as long
as spaghetti noodles, enters."

06:14.750 --> 06:16.747
Why don't you just take
your first call?

06:16.780 --> 06:18.377
Suicide hotline.

06:18.411 --> 06:21.239
Hey, I'm a pathetic dog
whose family kicked him out,

06:21.272 --> 06:22.703
and I want to kill myself.

06:22.736 --> 06:24.035
- Stewie?
- Hey, Brian!

06:24.068 --> 06:26.363
How's the new job going?

06:32.386 --> 06:33.717
All right, here comes the fight.

06:33.750 --> 06:35.813
Get ready to eat it, Drago!

06:38.209 --> 06:39.449
And Balboa is down!

06:39.473 --> 06:40.704
Drago wins!

06:42.534 --> 06:44.497
- What the hell?
- Son of a bitch!

06:44.530 --> 06:47.758
Those Ruski bastards changed
the movie so Drago wins!

06:47.791 --> 06:49.289
Yeah! Rocky gets up!

06:49.322 --> 06:50.986
Not only does
he not get up,

06:51.019 --> 06:54.479
he's holding a sign that says,
"Workers of the world, unite!"

06:54.512 --> 06:56.476
Well, that-that seems
like a logical idea,

06:56.509 --> 06:58.273
but this aggression
will not stand!

06:58.306 --> 07:01.135
I'm writing Vladimir Putin
an angry e-mail.

07:01.168 --> 07:02.731
"Dear Vladimir..."

07:02.764 --> 07:04.296
Ho-ho! That's telling him.

07:04.329 --> 07:06.392
"I hope this e-mail
finds you well."

07:06.425 --> 07:09.154
Oh, man, I wish
I could see his face.

07:09.187 --> 07:10.617
"I'll get right to the point.

07:10.650 --> 07:12.447
"My friends and I were aghast

07:12.480 --> 07:15.209
"when we saw what you did
to the end of Rocky IV.

07:15.242 --> 07:17.538
"Everyone knows
that any American

07:17.571 --> 07:20.101
"can beat up any Russian
on any day of the week.

07:20.134 --> 07:22.796
"Other than that,
all is well on this end.

07:22.829 --> 07:25.357
"Chris continues to hit
the books as best he can,

07:25.391 --> 07:27.887
"and his grades have shown
some improvement.

07:27.920 --> 07:29.883
"Stewie is growing like a weed.

07:29.916 --> 07:33.210
And Meg has become a woman
in front of our very eyes."

07:33.243 --> 07:35.339
And... send.

07:35.373 --> 07:39.233
I think we lost a little steam
there at the end.

07:43.093 --> 07:46.887
We now return to
Captain America: Civil Union.

07:46.920 --> 07:49.082
All right, Captain America,
we have to get ready

07:49.115 --> 07:50.713
for the big fight
with the other heroes.

07:50.747 --> 07:53.175
- Who do we have on our side?
- Well, Hawkeye, we've got you,

07:53.208 --> 07:56.170
Scarlet Witch, the Falcon,
and, of course, Randy.

07:56.202 --> 07:58.365
- Who's Randy?
- You know Randy.

07:58.398 --> 07:59.697
Lives in my guesthouse.

07:59.731 --> 08:00.993
We've been friends
since college.

08:00.994 --> 08:02.159
He's... my pal.

08:02.192 --> 08:03.823
He's the guy
I went to Paris with.

08:03.856 --> 08:05.519
You are such a coward!

08:05.552 --> 08:06.851
Randy!

08:11.575 --> 08:13.172
Vladimir Putin?!

08:13.206 --> 08:14.936
Da. Where is bathroom?

08:14.969 --> 08:16.533
I George Brett myself on plane.

08:17.066 --> 08:18.330
Gross!

08:18.363 --> 08:20.027
You can Google that
during the commercial.

08:26.882 --> 08:29.011
Oh, my God. President Putin?

08:29.044 --> 08:31.007
What-what are you doing here?

08:31.040 --> 08:32.937
Husband write me
impertinent e-mail.

08:32.971 --> 08:35.499
Says any American
can beat up any Russian.

08:35.531 --> 08:37.329
I am here to prove him wrong.

08:37.363 --> 08:39.459
You're gonna beat up my husband?

08:39.492 --> 08:41.821
Unless he American chicken.

08:43.152 --> 08:45.314
Did you just call me chicken?

08:45.348 --> 08:46.346
Yes. Chicken.

08:46.347 --> 08:48.143
Fi-cray! Fi-cray! Fi-cray!

08:48.176 --> 08:50.106
Sound different in Russia.

08:50.140 --> 08:53.267
Nobody calls me... chicken.

08:53.300 --> 08:55.196
Outside, now.

08:55.230 --> 08:57.627
Hi, we're from
Publishers Clearing House.

08:57.660 --> 09:01.519
I have a million-dollar check
for someone named Chicken.

09:01.552 --> 09:03.949
A conflict!

09:05.478 --> 09:06.943
You're going down!

09:06.976 --> 09:09.072
- Kick his ass, Peter!
- Yeah, kick his ass!

09:09.106 --> 09:10.803
Punch his ass, Peter!

09:15.294 --> 09:17.092
Oh, pretty quick, huh?

09:17.125 --> 09:19.088
Well, how about this?

09:20.751 --> 09:22.382
Here comes the haymaker!

09:27.706 --> 09:29.136
You had enough?

09:31.699 --> 09:33.295
He gone.

09:33.328 --> 09:34.894
Peter!

09:34.927 --> 09:37.322
Oh, looks like Putin's phone
is buzzing.

09:46.805 --> 09:49.101
Brian?

09:49.135 --> 09:51.531
Oh, hey, Marth... a.

09:51.564 --> 09:53.759
- What are you doing here?
- I'm always here.

09:53.792 --> 09:56.421
Suicide is not
a nine-to-five problem.

09:57.453 --> 09:59.083
Yeah, so I was thinking,

09:59.117 --> 10:01.179
maybe we could
Netflix and grill.

10:01.213 --> 10:03.275
I think it's
"Netflix and chill."

10:03.309 --> 10:05.937
Oh. Good,
'cause I don't have a grill.

10:05.970 --> 10:07.503
Hey, do you have Netflix?

10:07.536 --> 10:09.164
The credit card numbers
I've been guessing

10:09.165 --> 10:10.163
keep getting rejected.

10:10.197 --> 10:12.892
Good night, Brian.

10:12.925 --> 10:16.252
Well, nothing says
I can't date her up here.

10:16.286 --> 10:20.212
Let's see what kind of Facebook
account we got for this Martha.

10:20.245 --> 10:21.710
Uhp, private account.

10:21.743 --> 10:23.606
But... sister.

10:23.639 --> 10:26.701
Similar age. Few parties
they went to together.

10:26.734 --> 10:28.764
Ooh, "Grandpa's Funeral."

10:28.797 --> 10:31.259
Baby look good in black.

10:31.292 --> 10:33.121
That's her mom?

10:33.155 --> 10:35.817
Damn. I can work with this.

10:40.708 --> 10:43.438
You know, this is exactly what
Dr. Fishbein was talking about.

10:43.471 --> 10:45.467
I never go for it.

10:47.597 --> 10:49.227
♪ Martha ♪

10:49.260 --> 10:52.055
♪ You're playing hide and seek ♪

10:52.088 --> 10:54.318
♪ With love ♪

10:54.351 --> 10:55.649
♪ Martha ♪

10:55.681 --> 10:57.812
♪ This is what Dr. Fishbein ♪

10:57.845 --> 11:00.673
♪ Was talking about ♪

11:00.706 --> 11:02.504
♪ Martha ♪

11:02.537 --> 11:04.166
♪ With a little bit of love ♪

11:04.200 --> 11:06.162
♪ And a whole lot of sass... ♪

11:06.196 --> 11:07.561
You know what, Brian, I will...

11:07.595 --> 11:09.257
Oh, my God!

11:12.419 --> 11:14.882
Gross! You scumbag!

11:14.915 --> 11:18.475
♪ Dr. Fishbein predicted it'd be
three years of treatment ♪

11:18.508 --> 11:21.635
♪ And Martha's
only six months in... ♪

11:21.669 --> 11:24.031
Come on, Marth... a.

11:24.065 --> 11:26.627
♪ Martha ♪

11:26.660 --> 11:28.657
♪ It's gonna work out. ♪

11:33.315 --> 11:35.445
I'll tell you something,
if he were here right now,

11:35.478 --> 11:36.509
I'd kick his ass.

11:36.543 --> 11:38.140
Just like hundreds
of dead journalists,

11:38.172 --> 11:40.269
I'm not afraid
of Vladimir Putin.

11:40.303 --> 11:43.530
Hello?
Is it me you're looking for?

11:45.428 --> 11:46.458
Yes!

11:50.419 --> 11:52.247
Peter, you not coward I thought.

11:52.281 --> 11:53.977
You put up impressive fight.

11:54.011 --> 11:55.542
Thanks, Vladimir.

11:55.575 --> 11:57.439
You know, as someone
who doesn't read the paper

11:57.472 --> 11:59.967
or listen to the news,
you're not such a bad guy.

12:00.001 --> 12:01.131
Well, thank you.

12:01.164 --> 12:02.962
To show there are
no hard feelings,

12:02.996 --> 12:04.892
anyone want to go to strip club

12:04.925 --> 12:07.221
and look at some cat emojis
with me?

12:07.254 --> 12:09.417
- Hell yeah.
- I'm up for the strip club.

12:09.450 --> 12:11.180
Great. Who's driving?

12:11.213 --> 12:13.909
You know, you're gonna think I'm
crazy, but it's such a nice day,

12:13.941 --> 12:16.104
I was kind of thinking
of taking my shirt off

12:16.137 --> 12:17.270
and riding a horse there.

12:17.303 --> 12:18.700
Get out.

12:18.733 --> 12:20.730
That's totally my thing!

12:23.758 --> 12:26.985
Ah, the sun feels good
on my drunk chest.

12:27.018 --> 12:29.249
You know what,
you're a good guy, Peter.

12:29.282 --> 12:30.413
Friend?

12:30.447 --> 12:32.343
How do you say
"friend" in Russian?

12:32.376 --> 12:33.906
There is no Russian word for it.

12:33.940 --> 12:36.535
Well, you're my friend now.
Funny how this worked out.

12:36.568 --> 12:37.866
Who would have thought, huh?

12:37.899 --> 12:40.395
I guess things not always
what they seem.

12:40.429 --> 12:43.722
Yeah. I mean, except for
Ronan Farrow, who is clearly

12:43.755 --> 12:47.116
Woody Allen's son and
absolutely not Frank Sinatra's.

12:47.149 --> 12:49.512
I.. You know, I-I'm glad
you could make it home

12:49.545 --> 12:50.975
for the family dinner, Ronan.

12:51.009 --> 12:53.207
You got it, four eyes.
Wouldn't miss a dinner

12:53.240 --> 12:55.535
with my cuckoo dad
for the world.

12:55.568 --> 12:57.863
Hey, Anna May Wong,
no tickie, no shirtie.

12:57.897 --> 13:00.693
I'm just kidding around,
rice bowl. Geez, lighten up.

13:00.726 --> 13:03.289
This room is tighter
than Ava Gardner's caboose.

13:03.321 --> 13:04.651
Us, right?

13:04.685 --> 13:07.314
It's like lookin' in a mirror.

13:11.306 --> 13:13.735
Well, Peter, thank you
for showing me Quahog.

13:13.768 --> 13:15.000
Ah, it was fun.

13:15.032 --> 13:16.664
I'm gonna miss you, Vladimir.

13:16.696 --> 13:18.427
So come with me back to Russia.

13:18.461 --> 13:19.658
I need friend.

13:19.691 --> 13:22.220
Ah, I'm flattered,
but my home is here.

13:22.254 --> 13:23.950
And besides,
I can't go to Russia.

13:23.983 --> 13:25.814
I'm scared of Brigitte Nielsen.

13:25.848 --> 13:27.644
She is here with you
in your country.

13:27.677 --> 13:28.808
She-she's here now?
Is she...

13:28.841 --> 13:30.440
O... All ri...
Okay, okay, let's go.

13:30.473 --> 13:32.835
Let's go, let's go, let's go,
wheels up, let's go!

13:35.596 --> 13:38.058
Oh, my God, she can smell
the tiny bottles of booze.

13:38.092 --> 13:40.322
We got to go!
We got to go now!

13:48.573 --> 13:51.933
Dear Lord, please send me
a six-foot-seven blonde woman

13:51.966 --> 13:54.995
who likes to drink
until she blacks out.

13:55.028 --> 13:58.123
I think
we got our prayers crossed.

14:10.501 --> 14:12.664
Welcome to Russia, Peter.

14:12.697 --> 14:16.357
Man, Russia has the hottest
and ugliest women in the world.

14:16.390 --> 14:17.954
All tens and ones.

14:17.987 --> 14:20.117
Wow! Whoa.

14:20.151 --> 14:21.547
Wow!
Whoa.

14:21.580 --> 14:24.508
- Wow! Whoa.
- Whoa.

14:24.542 --> 14:26.604
Aw, I'm a "whoa."

14:26.638 --> 14:28.203
I know what'll cheer you up.

14:28.236 --> 14:30.931
We listen to funny
morning zoo on radio.

14:30.964 --> 14:33.826
You're listening
to backwards-K-FMB.

14:33.859 --> 14:36.421
I am The Penis,
here with Buttocks.

14:36.454 --> 14:38.484
Hello, Buttocks.

14:38.518 --> 14:40.248
Ha. Humor.

14:40.281 --> 14:43.342
Now time for government-
approved prank phone call.

14:49.298 --> 14:50.729
What?

14:50.762 --> 14:52.093
Is your refrigerator running?

14:52.126 --> 14:53.457
Yes.

14:53.491 --> 14:55.487
You are very fortunate.

14:59.147 --> 15:02.042
I've tried everything, Lou.
I told her I was sorry.

15:02.076 --> 15:03.606
I even sent flowers.

15:03.639 --> 15:05.434
She's gonna report me,
and I'm gonna get fired.

15:05.436 --> 15:06.633
Wh-What can I do?

15:06.667 --> 15:08.863
Do what I do when people
don't pay their rent:

15:08.896 --> 15:10.860
plant drugs and call the cops.

15:10.893 --> 15:12.523
I don't know, I-I may be broke,

15:12.557 --> 15:15.185
but that seems like a
crappy thing to do to somebody.

15:15.218 --> 15:16.715
Well, then you're evicted.

15:16.749 --> 15:18.413
Okay, fine.

15:18.446 --> 15:20.077
But where am I gonna get drugs?

15:20.109 --> 15:22.804
Walk me to my car.
My trunk is full of coke.

15:27.430 --> 15:28.761
Brian Griffin?

15:28.794 --> 15:30.790
Your life's about to change.

15:32.753 --> 15:34.151
Brian Griffin?

15:34.184 --> 15:36.913
We're not having
a lot of luck today.

15:42.170 --> 15:43.666
So, what do you do for fun
around here?

15:43.667 --> 15:45.498
- You got DirecTV?
- We have Time Warner.

15:45.531 --> 15:47.128
- You got HBO?
- We have Starz.

15:47.161 --> 15:49.324
- You got ESPN?
- We have Fox Sports 1.

15:49.357 --> 15:51.154
Does that come in HD?

15:51.188 --> 15:52.518
You got...

15:52.551 --> 15:55.712
Everything you say, I say
something little bit worse.

15:55.745 --> 15:58.042
- You got Simpsons?
- We have Family Guy.

15:58.076 --> 16:00.205
Ah, I did it to myself.

16:03.532 --> 16:05.428
Well, just shoot her first.

16:05.462 --> 16:06.926
It's not called
"suicide-murder,"

16:06.960 --> 16:08.656
it's called "murder-suicide."

16:08.689 --> 16:10.853
Brian, can I talk to you
for a second?

16:10.886 --> 16:13.082
- Yeah, sure.
- I wanted to tell you,

16:13.115 --> 16:15.577
I thought a lot about
what happened, and I guess...

16:15.610 --> 16:19.104
In your own weird way...
You were complimenting me.

16:19.138 --> 16:21.600
Um, w... w-what?

16:25.626 --> 16:28.255
I just wanted to let you know
I'm not going to tell anyone

16:28.288 --> 16:29.952
about what happened, and...

16:29.984 --> 16:32.847
maybe we could
get that drink tomorrow.

16:35.109 --> 16:36.972
Tell 'em you have no idea
how your hair strands

16:37.006 --> 16:38.803
got in that baggie.
Hello, Officer!

16:38.836 --> 16:41.730
- Is this your desk, ma'am?
- Yeah. Why, Officer?

16:41.764 --> 16:42.961
Found it.

16:42.995 --> 16:45.224
- What is that?
- Like you don't know.

16:45.257 --> 16:48.286
Cocaine.
Glorious cocaine.

16:48.319 --> 16:50.082
Best thing ever.

16:50.115 --> 16:51.846
You're gonna
have to come with us.

16:51.880 --> 16:54.176
And, Jeff, you might
want to call your sponsor.

16:54.209 --> 16:55.572
You did this, didn't you?

16:55.605 --> 16:58.101
I knew you were a little twerp
as soon as I met you.

16:58.134 --> 16:59.898
He did this!
He planted that!

16:59.931 --> 17:01.263
Martha, I'm so sorr...

17:01.296 --> 17:02.826
You bastard!

17:05.188 --> 17:07.052
Aah! My leg is broken!

17:07.085 --> 17:10.080
Only thing I can possibly do
is lick it repeatedly.

17:14.339 --> 17:16.336
There we go.
That's fixing it.

17:23.223 --> 17:25.219
Please pass the aspic.

17:27.648 --> 17:29.644
I'll have the aspic.

17:30.743 --> 17:33.805
I, too, will have the aspic.

17:33.838 --> 17:35.777
Could you
please pass the beef jelly?

17:38.362 --> 17:40.026
Huh? See?

17:40.059 --> 17:42.454
Now aren't you glad
we did all that work earlier?

17:42.488 --> 17:44.319
Peter, come.

17:44.352 --> 17:47.512
Over here is where
we rig every American election.

17:47.545 --> 17:48.778
Eh.

17:48.811 --> 17:51.007
Also, American football.

17:51.040 --> 17:52.237
What?! No!

17:52.271 --> 17:55.232
Is true. Meet my best friend,
Roger Goodell.

17:55.266 --> 17:57.427
NFL Commissioner Roger Goodell?

17:57.461 --> 17:58.993
You're a Russian spy?

17:59.026 --> 18:00.757
I don't know, Peter.

18:00.789 --> 18:02.619
Why don't you tell me?

18:02.653 --> 18:05.281
Today we decide
which New England Patriot

18:05.314 --> 18:06.779
to suspend, eh?

18:06.812 --> 18:09.906
Da. Tom Brady or Tom Brady?

18:17.626 --> 18:20.354
You leave that gorgeous
piece of ass alone.

18:20.387 --> 18:22.284
I was right about you
from the start, Putin.

18:22.318 --> 18:24.380
You can't just do
whatever you want in the world

18:24.414 --> 18:25.578
and get away with it.

18:25.612 --> 18:27.941
It's time
someone stood up to you.

18:27.973 --> 18:29.671
And survived.

18:35.127 --> 18:38.689
Ladies and gentlemens,

18:38.722 --> 18:41.250
tonight we are here
to see the fight

18:41.284 --> 18:44.311
to determine
East/West superiority.

18:44.344 --> 18:46.175
Fighting for Russia,

18:46.208 --> 18:48.571
President Vladimir Putin!

18:50.900 --> 18:52.863
Fighting for America,

18:52.896 --> 18:56.357
Kevin James!

18:56.390 --> 18:58.886
Everybody here
thinks I'm Kevin James.

19:38.515 --> 19:41.477
Kevin James! Kevin James!

19:41.510 --> 19:42.915
- Kevin James!
- I can't believe it,

19:42.939 --> 19:44.404
but it sounds like the audience

19:44.438 --> 19:47.199
is starting to cheer
for the American!

19:47.232 --> 19:49.895
Kevin James! Kevin James!

19:54.219 --> 19:56.382
Enough!

19:58.579 --> 20:00.775
Lois?
What are you doing here?

20:00.808 --> 20:02.506
I'm not really here, Peter.

20:02.539 --> 20:04.201
You've been hit
several times in the head

20:04.235 --> 20:06.665
and sustained
severe brain trauma.

20:06.698 --> 20:09.160
She's right.
This has gone too far.

20:09.193 --> 20:11.523
There are other ways
to settle our differences.

20:11.556 --> 20:12.721
Say you.

20:12.754 --> 20:14.750
Yes. Say me.

20:16.280 --> 20:19.841
♪ Say you, say me ♪

20:21.671 --> 20:23.667
♪ Say it for always ♪

20:25.830 --> 20:27.993
♪ That's the way it should be ♪

20:28.026 --> 20:29.956
♪ So you think
you know the answers... ♪

20:29.990 --> 20:31.952
Vlad and I finished our dance,

20:31.986 --> 20:33.948
then spent the rest
of the night talking.

20:33.982 --> 20:37.110
The next day, he poisoned me
on the limo ride to the airport

20:37.143 --> 20:38.607
with radioactive tea.

20:38.640 --> 20:42.034
♪ Believing who you are ♪

20:42.068 --> 20:45.794
♪ You are a shining star... ♪

20:45.827 --> 20:48.023
I lost half
my body weight, all my hair,

20:48.057 --> 20:50.420
and I have lesions
that'll never heal.

20:50.453 --> 20:53.247
That's our president's
best friend.

20:53.280 --> 20:56.708
♪ Say you, say me. ♪

20:56.709 --> 21:57.540
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru